# Ignore file for `Dockerfile`, deliberately NOT named `.dockerignore`.
#
# core#1014. Neither of this project's two build paths has its context root at
# this directory, so a plain `.dockerignore` here is read by nobody:
#
#   GHA  (.github/workflows/build-push-image.yml)
#        context root = build-context/, this checkout = build-context/datanika/
#   box  (docker-compose.yml: `context: ..`)
#        context root = the monorepo root, which is outside every git repo and
#        therefore cannot hold a committed file at all
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile in preference
# to the context root's, and the Dockerfile is inside this checkout on BOTH paths.
# So this one file covers both. Measured on buildx 0.30 (`docker build`) and on
# Compose v2 (`docker compose build`), each with the ignore file renamed away as a
# negative control.
#
# 🚨 Patterns are matched against paths RELATIVE TO THE CONTEXT ROOT, which is a
# level above this file. A bare `.git` matches only `<context>/.git` and would NOT
# match `datanika-cloud/.git`. Every pattern here must stay recursive (`**/`).
# That is not tidiness: the image grafts the PRIVATE datanika-cloud tree at
# /cloud/, so an un-ignored `.git` publishes that repository's whole history the
# moment the package's visibility changes.

**/.git
**/.venv
**/.claude
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/htmlcov
**/.env
**/.env.docker
**/*.egg-info
